Embedded React: scale and convert only the clipped part of an image.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json. Changed files: engine/rendering/
image_scaler.c and engine/tests/rendering/test_image.c. Proposed upstream,
without the integer bilinear weights, as pull request #285.

render_region() produced every row of a scaled, tinted or CPU-converted RGB565
image on each repaint, then let the row blits discard what fell outside the
clip. A repaint touching a corner of a large image therefore paid for all of
it: about 30 ms per repaint for a 1280x600 image drawn at 1880x880 on an
Apple M4. Both paths now produce only the destination inside the active clip.
Bilinear sampling also computes the column taps once per call and blends with
8-bit integer weights, two channels per multiply, instead of per-pixel float
coordinates and weights; results differ from the float version by at most two
levels per channel, and opaque images stay exactly opaque. The new test checks
that a damage-clipped repaint over an upscaled and over an unscaled RGB565
image matches the full repaint and writes nothing outside the damage.

